('b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 1, 'pre_test', 'In chemical kinetics rate laws (Rate = k[A]ⁿ), what exponent (n) defines the quantitative mathematical sensitivity of reaction rate to changes in reactant concentration?', 'Rate Constant', 'Reaction Order', 'Planck''s Constant', 'Mass Defect Exponent', 'B', 'The reaction order indicates how many times over the rate increases relative to changes in reactant concentration.', 'assets/illustrations/term1/q36.svg', true),
