('b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 1, 'pre_test', 'What proportionality constant (k) in a rate law equation links reactant concentration terms directly to reaction velocity at a fixed temperature?', 'Universal Gas Constant (R)', 'Equilibrium Constant (Keq)', 'Rate Constant (k)', 'Acid Dissociation Constant (Ka)', 'C', 'The rate constant (k) is an intrinsic proportionality factor unique to a reaction at a specific temperature.', 'assets/illustrations/term1/q37.svg', true),
('b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 1, 'post_test', 'What proportionality constant (k) in a rate law equation links reactant concentration terms directly to reaction velocity at a fixed temperature?', 'Universal Gas Constant (R)', 'Equilibrium Constant (Keq)', 'Rate Constant (k)', 'Acid Dissociation Constant (Ka)', 'C', 'The rate constant (k) is an intrinsic proportionality factor unique to a reaction at a specific temperature.', 'assets/illustrations/term1/q37.svg', true),
('b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 1, 'pre_test', 'In a multi-step reaction mechanism, what specific elementary reaction step governs and limits the overall reaction rate?', 'Fast Equilibrium Step', 'Rate-Determining Step (RDS)', 'Chain Termination Step', 'Final Solvent Exchange Step', 'B', 'The slowest elementary step in a reaction sequence acts as a kinetic bottleneck, dictating the total reaction rate.', 'assets/illustrations/term1/q38.svg', true),
