('b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000106', 1, 'pre_test', 'Formulate the classification for a catalytic system where the catalyst exists in the exact same physical phase (e.g. liquid) as the reactants.', 'Heterogeneous Catalysis', 'Homogeneous Catalysis', 'Phase-Transfer Inhibition', 'Interfacial Adsorption', 'B', 'Homogeneous catalysis occurs when catalyst and reactants reside in a uniform single physical phase (e.g., aqueous acid catalyst in solution).', 'assets/illustrations/term1/q40.svg', true),
